the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 4.

the actions are:
    the move convert to tables is made; known as convert_to_tables.
    the move convert to triples is made; known as convert_to_triples.

the fluents are:
    *a thing* student *a second thing* with *a third thing* with *a fourth thing*; known as student.
    student.advisor; known as student.advisor.
    student.major; known as student.major.
    student.year; known as student.year.
    *a thing* is the student advisor of *a second thing*; known as student_advisor.
    *a thing* is the student major of *a second thing*; known as student_major.
    *a thing* is the student year of *a second thing*; known as student_year.

the knowledge base triples includes:

the text of the game is at "sources/triples.rules".

when the move convert to tables is made
    and a thing is the student major of a second thing
    and the thing is the student advisor of a third thing
    and the thing is the student year of a fourth thing
then the thing student the second thing with the third thing with the fourth thing.

when the move convert to tables is made
    and a thing is the student major of a second thing
then it is not the case that the thing is the student major of the second thing.

when the move convert to tables is made
    and a thing is the student advisor of a second thing
then it is not the case that the thing is the student advisor of the second thing.

when the move convert to tables is made
    and a thing is the student year of a second thing
then it is not the case that the thing is the student year of the second thing.

when the move convert to triples is made
    and a thing student a second thing with a third thing with a fourth thing
then the thing is the student major of the second thing
    and the thing is the student advisor of the third thing
    and the thing is the student year of the fourth thing
    and it is not the case that the thing student the second thing with the third thing with the fourth thing.

initially aaron student architecture with alan with freshman
    and belinda student computers with cathy with sophomore
    and calvin student english with donna with junior
    and george student physics with frank with senior.

% EpilogJS's state after the play (the twin's final state under LPS2 must be the same):
%   - student(aaron,architecture,alan,freshman)
%   - student(belinda,computers,cathy,sophomore)
%   - student(calvin,english,donna,junior)
%   - student(george,physics,frank,senior)
scenario play is:
    the move convert to triples is made from 1 to 2.
    the move convert to tables is made from 2 to 3.

